Newspaper clippings:

1. Download newspaper clippings from newspapers.com in this name format:

	The_Daily_Times_1901_04_17_03.jpg

2. Rename into standard format

	rename-news.sh *.jpg

2. Upload to File API

	gemini-files.sh --delete
	gemini-files.sh --upload *.jpg

3. Create OCR files

	gemini-files.sh --ocr all
	
Books:

1. Download book PDF in this format

	naturalhistoryse0000whit.pdf

2. pdfslice.sh into smaller PDF(s) with page range specified like this:

	naturalhistoryse0000whit_205-225.pdf

3. Rename to standard format:

	~/scripts/rename-ia.sh -d naturalhistoryse0000whit_205-225.pdf
	(the -d will add the date to the start of the filename)
	Output: '1789 +a White +b The Natural History of Selborne +p London; Benjamin White +n 205-225 +iaid naturalhistoryse0000whit.pdf'

4. Upload to File API

	gemini-files.sh --upload '1789 +a White +b The Natural History ...'

5. Create .ocr version

	gemini-files.sh --ocr '1789 +a White +b The Natural History ...'
	

Journals and web pages:

1. pdfslice.sh into smaller parts as needed
2. rename-ia.sh and manually enter metadata

