Create Cache File

0. cd to project directory containing .ocr files
1. awk 'FNR==1 {print "\n---------------------------------\nFile: " FILENAME "\n---------------------------------"} 1' *.ocr > all-ocr-project.txt
2. gemini-cache.sh all-ocr-project.txt
3. gemini-ask.sh query1.txt
   gemini-ask.sh query1.2.txt
   gemini-ask.sh query1.3.txt
   etc.. query1.txt will produce query1.out and keep a history. Then query1.2.txt will remember the conversation context in that thread.
   Each major number change eg. query2.txt will not remember the conversation with the query1.txt thread.
4. Rember! Cache only lasts 1 hour

Step 2 automates these steps:
 *. gemini-files.sh --delete all-ocr-project.txt
 *. gemini-files.sh --upload all-ocr-project.txt      (note the file ID)
 *. gemini-files.sh --create-cache <file ID>         (note the cache ID)
 *. gemini-files.sh --list-cache

Step 3 automates this step:
 *. gemini-files.sh --query <cache ID> --query-file query7.2.txt --use-history --history-file query7.json > query7.2.out ; cat query7.2.out
      query7.2.txt is where the prompt is written
      query7.json is the conversation history
      query7.2.out is the output of the query
      gemini-ask.sh learns the cache ID from a hidden file in the CWD as maintained by gemini-cache.sh

